From 7fbdb6eba98a967d56b24ddf0de1caf46f3ea679 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:32:07 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 45/48] Perf: a per-frame CSV and a stall sampler

<prefix>_PERF_CSV=<file> writes one row per present (interval, what it
showed: the flip's frame, a blended in-between frame, a frame as it is or
why interpolation refused; blend fraction, skipped grid moments, lateness,
rate) and one per game frame (guest, render, wait, pacing, GPU and the
emulation thread's CPU time; pipelines created and prewarmed, textures
decoded, texture-key hashing, render-target snapshots, interpolation's
pairing, presents not made), with the input script's scene as a column.

<prefix>_TRACE_STALL_SAMPLES[=ms] (Windows) samples the emulation
thread's host stack while a frame runs long, or with =present while a
present between flips is overdue, and prints the commonest stacks at the
next flip. The thread is stopped only to copy its registers and stack top;
the walk and the names come after it runs again.

Both off by default: each note is one test of a flag.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
