@@ -90,6 +90,8 @@ Every one of these takes the profile's own prefix, so `TENKAWA_TRACE_KERNEL` for
 | `<PREFIX>_TRACE_TRANSFERS` | Each GE block transfer (source, destination, rectangle) and whether it was also copied on the GPU, at the internal scale, into a target standing for the destination (`copy_block_transfer()` in `host/gpu/vulkan_renderer.cpp`), and once a display list whether a texture over such a copy sampled it. `<PREFIX>_NO_TRANSFER_TARGETS` copies in guest memory only (the texture then reads the 1x read-back), as before; `<PREFIX>_TRANSFER_SAMPLED_KEY` keys textures over the latest transfers' destinations by one word in 256, as before, instead of every byte |
 | `<PREFIX>_TRACE_ENV_MAP[=N]` | The first N draws (40 by default) in texture map mode 2, environment (shade) mapping: the lights 0xC1 names and their vectors, the world matrix, the texture scale and offset, the first vertices. The vertex shader makes U and V from the world-space normal and the two lights' vectors (`environment_map_uv()` in `host/gpu/shaders/ge.vert`); `<PREFIX>_NO_ENV_MAP` uses the vertex UVs, as before; `<PREFIX>_ENV_MAP_OFFSET` adds the texture offset to the coordinates it makes |
 | `<PREFIX>_TRACE_SAS` | SAS voices set, keyed on and off, and each change of the end flags a game polls |
+| `<PREFIX>_PERF_CSV=<file>` | One CSV row per present (time, interval, what it showed: the flip's frame, a blended in-between frame, a frame as it is, or why interpolation refused; blend fraction, grid moments skipped, lateness, rate) and one per game frame (guest, render, wait, pacing and GPU time, the emulation thread's CPU time, pipelines created and their time, pipelines the prewarm had ready, textures decoded and their time, texture-key hashing time, render-target snapshots and their size, interpolation's pairing, presents not made); the input script's `scene NAME` is a column (`host/perf/frame_stats.hpp`) |
+| `<PREFIX>_TRACE_STALL_SAMPLES[=ms]` | Windows: while a game frame takes longer than the threshold (50 ms by default), sample the emulation thread's host stack every few milliseconds and print the commonest stacks at the next flip, with names when the program's PDB is beside it (link with `/DEBUG`). `=present` samples while a present between flips is more than 2 ms overdue instead |
 | `<PREFIX>_NO_BUSY_CLOCK` | Keep emulated time still for a thread that never waits, as before the busy clock (`Kernel::charge_busy_time`) |
 | `PSPRECOMP_NO_INTERPRETER=1` | Turn the interpreter off. Nothing runs without a corpus; with one, the runtime stops at the first address the recompiler missed and names it |
 | `PSPRECOMP_MAX_DISPATCHES` | Stop after this many dispatches, for a bounded run |
